SurveillanceHound — always-running NVR / IP-camera network monitor.

Watches the surveillance segment (camera VLAN, NVR uplink, or a SPAN port)
for activity the surveillance threat model cares about: bulk transfers
toward a camera (firmware push), long-lived camera↔public sessions on
non-routine ports (control-channel-shaped), off-allowlist telemetry,
new devices, new peers, silent cameras, and behavioral anomalies vs each
camera's learned per-(weekday, hour) baseline.

Per-camera ring buffer + on-alert pcap snapshots for forensic review.
Pluggable notification channels: stdout, logfile, jsonlines, webhook,
syslog (RFC 5424 UDP/TCP), email (SMTP), FTP/FTPS. A built-in read-only
web dashboard renders the live state with a dark cyberpunk theme.

WWW: https://github.com/RNAX0N/surveillancehound
